From e75ef7506c13c56e584f03f4e076c9f4afa13c9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vedantpatil04 <vedantpatil513@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 04:19:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix: align driver login with the API's expiresAt contract

The login endpoint returns an absolute expiresAt, but the mobile session
store read a relative expiresIn that the API never sent, so a real device
login failed while unit tests (which mocked the assumed shape) passed.

- mobile session store prefers expiresAt, falling back to expiresIn
- auth response also carries expiresIn for older clients
- API URL is derived from Metro's LAN host on physical devices
- dev-only logging of the failing login target
- demo seed creates driver logins (passcode from SEED_DRIVER_PASSWORD)
- expo start binds to the LAN host; IDE folders are ignored

Carried forward from local work in progress before Phase 3.
