From 1e7b9630f07ab5dce1bd419b4a39be1dd6235191 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vedantpatil04 <vedantpatil513@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:23:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat: implement fuel and daily operations

Phase 3: petrol/diesel as the driver's primary daily workflow, plus RTO,
tyre, tyre insurance and maintenance/service, with offline-safe submission,
receipts, admin review and Indian financial-year statements.

Database (additive migration; no existing data changed)
- fuel_entries and vehicle_expenses, linked to driver and vehicle through
  composite (company_id, id) foreign keys so cross-tenant rows cannot exist.
- Idempotency keys (company_id, client_submission_id) on fuel, expenses and
  documents. Documents gain a premium amount for tyre insurance.
- CHECK constraints: positive amounts and litres (which also makes the
  derived rate's division safe), consistent archive state.
- Indexes for company-wide date ranges and per-vehicle/per-driver history.

Backend
- Driver fuel entry: the server takes driver and vehicle from the session
  and current assignment; a vehicle sent by the app is rejected. The rate is
  derived as amount / litres on every read and never stored.
- Financial-year helper (1 Apr - 31 Mar) with India-time "today", so a UTC
  server cannot misfile an entry made just after midnight IST.
- Weighted average = total amount / total litres, in Decimal.
- Idempotent create: retries, and even simultaneous retries, store once.
- Receipt upload through the existing storage abstraction; identical bytes
  from the same uploader de-duplicate; drivers open only their own receipts.
- RTO, tyre and maintenance as vehicle expenses; tyre insurance stored as a
  TYRE_INSURANCE document with expiry, ready for the compliance phase.
- Office review: statement filters, period summaries, breakdowns, audited
  corrections, archive-with-reason and restore instead of delete.
- Login's expiresIn now comes from configuration rather than a literal.
- No AI is called; service receipts are stored as originals for later.

Web
- Parking, food and repair removed from types, constants, seed, reports and
  all six locales; RTO, tyre, tyre insurance and maintenance replace them.
  Demo store version bumped so stale local data resets instead of crashing.
- Admin Fuel: today / month / financial-year metrics, the FY statement with
  driver, vehicle, fuel type and station filters, receipts, archive, and
  PDF/Excel export through the existing exporters.
- Admin operations in the existing Expenses route; vehicle detail gains
  service history and tyre insurance. No new tabs.

Mobile
- Fuel form with only fuel type, amount, litres, station, date (today by
  default, editable) and receipt; recent-station suggestions.
- RTO, tyre, maintenance and tyre insurance forms; fuel history; the
  Updates tab in the final structure; ADD FUEL live; real daily summary.
- Offline-safe saving: queued before any network call, one submission id
  per form, plain-language "Saved / Will sync" states.
- Offline queue fix: temporary failures are now retried indefinitely
  instead of being discarded after five attempts; server rejections are
  kept and shown; an expired session pauses sync without losing entries.
- Receipts copied to app storage so Android cannot clear them before
  upload; fuel photos compressed, official documents kept at full quality.
- Session user type corrected to the API's real shape.
- Contract tests replay real captured API responses through mobile code.
